Kyng Chaos said:

> On the Qt-Mac Nethack it always defaults to filling the whole screen 
> with the window (not 'fullscreen' mode), and stretches the tiles to 
> some size (16x30 for me), which causes some scrolling of the map.  And 
> the Qt fontsize defaults to 'Huge'.

You want to set these Qt options in the NetHack configuration file:

    Qt_fontSize
    Qt_tileHeight
    Qt_tileWidth

On my machine -- 15" Aluminum PowerBook with Absurd tile set -- I
specify

    Qt_fontSize=large
    Qt_tileHeight=40 
    Qt_tileWidth=40


You cannot set these options in the NETHACKOPTIONS environment variable;
instead you must set them in the configuration file, which on Mac OS X
can be named either

    ~/Library/Preferences/NetHack Defaults

or

    ~/Library/Preferences/NetHack Defaults.txt

> This also seems to be independent of the tile_width and tile_height 
> options for nethack

Right. tile_width and tile_height specify the actual physical dimension
of each tile as laid out in the tiles file. Qt_tileHeight and
Qt_tileWidth specify how to *display* each tile. In my case, the Absurd
tiles have a physical size of 64x64, so I specify tile_height:64 and
tile_width:64. Through experimentation I know that a tile display size
of 40 suits me best with this tile set -- hence my Qt_xxx settings.

